Step 1 — Create the TriggerBinding "ui-triggerbinding.yaml"

Apply: oc apply -f ui\ui-triggerbinding.yaml
Expected: triggerbinding.triggers.tekton.dev/ui-triggerbinding created

oc get triggerbinding
NAME                AGE
ui-triggerbinding   19s

Step 2 — Create ui-triggertemplate.yaml
The TriggerTemplate's job is:
Take the values from TriggerBinding and create a new PipelineRun.

So our flow becomes:
        GitHub webhook
              ↓
        TriggerBinding
              ↓
        repo-url + revision
              ↓
        TriggerTemplate
              ↓
        ui-pipeline-run-xxxxx
              ↓
        clone → image-build → deploy

Apply: oc apply -f ui\ui-triggertemplate.yaml
Expected: triggertemplate.triggers.tekton.dev/ui-triggertemplate created

oc get triggertemplate
NAME                 AGE
ui-triggertemplate   25s

Step 3 — Create ui-trigger.yaml
Trigger ka kaam hai Binding aur Template ko connect karna:

Apply: oc apply -f ui\ui-trigger.yaml
Expected: trigger.triggers.tekton.dev/ui-trigger created

oc get tri
NAME         AGE
ui-trigger   3m6s

Step 4 — Create the EventListener "ui-eventlistener.yaml"

The EventListener says:
"When an HTTP event comes to me, send it to ui-triggerbinding and ui-triggertemplate."

So,
                GitHub
                   │
                   │ HTTP POST
                   ▼
                ui-eventlistener
                   │
                   ▼
                ui-triggerbinding
                   │
                   ▼
                ui-triggertemplate
                   │
                   ▼
                PipelineRun

Apply: oc apply -f ui\ui-eventlistener.yaml
Expected: eventlistener.triggers.tekton.dev/ui-eventlistener created

oc get eventlisteners
