Get the exact URL
oc get route ui-eventlistener -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}'
Expected: ui-eventlistener-amirahmad2204-dev.apps.rm3.7wse.p1.openshiftapps.com

Then the webhook URL will be:
https://ui-eventlistener-amirahmad2204-dev.apps.rm3.7wse.p1.openshiftapps.com
This is the URL to which GitHub will eventually send the webhook.

Step 6 - First Test — Send a POST Request
Before configuring GitHub, we manually tested the EventListener.

curl.exe -i -X POST "https://ui-eventlistener-amirahmad2204-dev.apps.rm3.7wse.p1.openshiftapps.com" `
-H "Content-Type: application/json" `
-d '{"ref":"refs/heads/feature/openshift","repository":{"clone_url":"https://github.com/amir35/tutorial-system.git"}}'

We got: HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
with: Invalid event body format

Step 7 - Create JSON Body Properly in PowerShell
Instead of directly putting the JSON into curl, we created a PowerShell object:

$body = @{
    ref = "refs/heads/feature/openshift"
    repository = @{
        clone_url = "https://github.com/amir35/tutorial-system.git"
    }
} | ConvertTo-Json -Compress

$body
Expected: {"ref":"refs/heads/feature/openshift","repository":{"clone_url":"https://github.com/amir35/tutorial-system.git"}}

Also, our git-clone-task.yaml was receiving branch name as refs/heads/feature/openshift.
So, we updated it to remove refs/heads/.

oc apply -f tasks\git-clone-task.yaml
Expected: task.tekton.dev/git-clone-task configured

Step 8 - We again sent the request using Invoke-RestMethod Instead
Invoke-RestMethod `
    -Uri "https://ui-eventlistener-amirahmad2204-dev.apps.rm3.7wse.p1.openshiftapps.com" `
    -Method POST `
    -ContentType "application/json" `
    -Body $body

Output:
